## Native model orchestration

Outside the shared Grok effort and review rules, choose the agent prompt, model, and
reasoning effort independently. Do not map models permanently to roles such as
scout, architect, or coder.

`pi-kit` lanes require an explicit full model selector and effort per call.

Available managed pool:

{{ template "model-table.md" }}

`Start` is an initial effort prior. `Cost` is relative marginal routing cost
(1 = cheapest). Scores are comparative routing context, not permanent roles.
Grok stays at high; adjust other efforts to task uncertainty.

Prefer Pi-native subagents over launching `claude`, `codex`, `grok`, or
`ollama` CLIs from inside Pi. Keep the CLIs for provider-native features or
when operating from another harness.

The main model owns scope, model selection, synthesis, validation, and the
final answer. Use parallel subagents only for genuinely independent work.

